  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>For questions 1 - 5, the standard form of an equation is \(ax^2+bx+c\). For each expression, find the missing constant \(c\) that would make the expression a perfect square.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="b7e7ca41-1fc8-45f8-8010-7bf1b5299f79" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--1a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="74779890-74be-4c6e-abac-e9c6c8418736" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="9">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2−6x+ \underline{\;\;c\;\;}\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 9 can be added to make the expression a perfect square.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="aff55de0-7356-4328-86a8-3cef24731e96" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="1">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2+2x+ \underline{\;\;c\;\;}\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 1 can be added to make the expression a perfect square.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="3e35319d-0d6b-4438-b898-a83eb4302848" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="49">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2+14x+ \underline{\;\;c\;\;}\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 49 can be added to make the expression a perfect square.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1d-->
  <exercise data-content-id="9dad8fdb-86ab-4fc5-91d4-2374565cfed6" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="4">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2−4x+ \underline{\;\;c\;\;}\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 4 can be added to make the expression a perfect square.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1e-->
  <exercise data-content-id="76a7bb49-df6b-4f07-9e91-fa1907096032" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="144">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2+24x+ \underline{\;\;c\;\;}\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 144 can be added to make the expression a perfect square.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="1a8021f2-29b7-460c-a547-5ada95fee16f" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-3">
    <problem>
      <para>If \(x^2−6x+c\) is factored to be \((x \_\_\_\_\_)^2\), what is the missing value of the factored form of this expression? Remember to include the sign.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! -3 </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.2.2 and 9.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="d27cd74b-c244-438d-95bf-926db14292d5" data-problem-comparator="text" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="+1">
    <problem>
      <para>If \(x^2+2x+c\) is factored to be \((x \_\_\_\_\_)^2\), what is the missing value of the factored form of this expression? Remember to include the sign.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! +1 </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="34d2148f-1960-4081-8dd9-f3562a759993" data-problem-comparator="text" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="+7">
    <problem>
      <para>If \(x^2+14x+c\) is factored to be \((x \_\_\_\_\_)^2\), what is the missing value of the factored form of this expression? Remember to enter the sign.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! +7</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2d-->
  <exercise data-content-id="0caa8b15-aa41-4a47-895e-6465577e9e88" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-2">
    <problem>
      <para>If \(x^2−4x+c\) is factored to be \((x \_\_\_\_\_)^2\), what is the missing value of the factored form of this expression? Remember to enter the sign.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! -2 </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2e-->
  <exercise data-content-id="c08b5393-28bf-4e98-96e0-02d1f5945809" data-problem-comparator="text" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="+12">
    <problem>
      <para>If \(x^2+24x+c\) is factored to be \((x \_\_\_\_\_)^2\), what is the missing value of the factored form of this expression? Remember to enter the sign.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! +12</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div>
</div>
<!--3a-->
<para>For each equation in questions 11 - 14, use the following scenario.</para>
<blockquote>
  <para>Jada looks at Mai's work and is confused. She doesn't see how Mai got her answer.</para>
  <para>Complete Mai's missing steps by answering the questions to help Jada see how Mai solved the equation.</para>
</blockquote>
<para>\(x^2+12x=13\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 1 - </emphasis>\(x^2\;+\;12x\; +\) \(\_\_\_\_\_\) \(=\;13\;+\) \(\_\_\_\_\_\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> \((x+6)^2=49\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 3 - </emphasis>\(\sqrt{(x+6)^2}=\sqrt{49}\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 4 -</emphasis> \(x+6= \pm\) \(\_\_\_\_\_\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 5 - </emphasis>\(x+6=\) \(\_\_\_\_\_\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 6 -</emphasis> \(x\;+\;6=\) \(-\) \(\_\_\_\_\_\)</para>
<para>\(x=1\) or \(x=-13\)</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="cfbe1b75-2465-4e60-a1b3-388b6e74600f" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="daff277b-a353-4044-96ee-ad9ea59081f8" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="36">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the missing term in Step 1?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 36</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="27ace37f-eb5a-468d-97a5-f15cc4b7470f" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="7">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the missing term in Steps 4, 5, and 6?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 7</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="c07dfbfc-4a8b-4a72-91ec-f847b6fad843" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="1">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the value of \(x\) in Step 5?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 1</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3d-->
  <exercise data-content-id="c88b63c7-9f5e-4680-8d0e-da4c7639548c" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-13">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the value of \(x\) in Step 6?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! -13</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div>
</div>
<para>For questions 15 - 20, solve choose the equivalent equation with a perfect square on one side.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="fe39100b-8e81-46fa-960e-0b0082305d03" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--4a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a68974c6-171a-48d6-8ba7-8ee9f75aedfa" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="5" data-solution="\((x+4)^2=18\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((x−7)^2=54\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+5)^2=12\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x−10)^2=91\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+4)^2=18\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+1)^2=1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+2)^2=9\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2+8x=2\) </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \((x+4)^2=18\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--4b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="69d3ec36-966a-47c0-9312-eb11834874ef" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="5" data-solution="\((x+5)^2=12\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((x−7)^2=54\\) &quot;, &quot;\\((x+5)^2=12\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x−10)^2=91\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+4)^2=18\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+1)^2=1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+2)^2=9\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2+10x=-13\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \((x+5)^2=12\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--4c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e21c7ba8-89c4-44ee-815e-7ba383005675" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="5" data-solution="\((x−7)^2=54\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((x−7)^2=54\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+5)^2=12\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x−10)^2=91\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+4)^2=18\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+1)^2=1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+2)^2=9\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2−14x=5\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \((x−7)^2=54\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--4d-->
  <exercise data-content-id="38c7644a-a7e8-4d2f-9bd0-dcf06b374b59" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="5" data-solution="\((x+1)^2=1\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((x−7)^2=54\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+5)^2=12\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x−10)^2=91\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+4)^2=18\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+1)^2=1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+2)^2=9\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2+2x=0\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \((x+1)^2=1\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--4e-->
  <exercise data-content-id="802db0f9-423e-49e8-a434-b7ddff12b747" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="5" data-solution="\((x+2)^2=9\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((x−7)^2=54\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+5)^2=12\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x−10)^2=91\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+4)^2=18\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+1)^2=1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+2)^2=9\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2+4x−5=0\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \((x+2)^2=9\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--4f-->
  <exercise data-content-id="c20e168d-e932-42c0-a244-a690ebff838c" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="5" data-solution="\((x−10)^2=91\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((x−7)^2=54\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+5)^2=12\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x−10)^2=91\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+4)^2=18\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+1)^2=1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x+2)^2=9\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2−20x=-9\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \((x−10)^2=91\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <solution> </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div>
</div>
<!--5a-->
<para>For questions 21-23, solve each equation by completing the square, then choose the <emphasis>two</emphasis> roots.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="d0369d05-5376-4ac1-b409-62e0acabf31a" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="01ba74f0-4495-49ae-a6f3-b852b9226b0d" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;\\(x = -1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 7\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(x = -1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 5\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 7\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 6\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2−6x+5=12\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(x=-1\) and \(x=7\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--5b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="026ea025-d407-4e51-ad91-854415e91c82" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;\\(x = -2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 4\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(x = 9\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = -2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 8\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 3\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 4\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2−2x=8\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(x=-2\) and \(x=4\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--5c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="cc4974dc-f7ef-4f80-b674-84e87c241f3c" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;\\(x = -6\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 2\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(x = 14\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 110\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = -6\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 4\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(11=x^2+4x−1\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(x=-6\) and \(x=2\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="b1e1f763-6ea6-46bd-8a02-8cd017f9bc9b" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="4" data-solution="\(x = 9\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(x = -21\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 9\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 39\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 78\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = -39\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Solve the equation \(x^2−18x+60=-21\) by completing the square.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(x=9\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div>
